COMMAND NAME: gpmigrator

Upgrades an existing Greenplum Database 3.x system to 3.2.

*****************************************************
SYNOPSIS
*****************************************************

gpmigrator <old_GPHOME_path> <new_GPHOME_path> 
[-d <master_data_directory>] [-l <logfile_directory>] [-q]

gpmigrator --version | --help


*****************************************************
PREREQUISITES
*****************************************************

The following are required prior to running this upgrade utility:

* Check for and recover any failed segments in your current 
  Greenplum Database system.

* Make sure both the old and new versions of the Greenplum Database 
  software are installed on all hosts (master and segments).

* Shut down your current Greenplum Database system.

* Make sure you are logged in to the master host as the 
  Greenplum Database superuser (gpadmin).

* Set $GPHOME to point to the new Greenplum Database software 
  version before running this utility.

*****************************************************
DESCRIPTION
*****************************************************

The gpmigrator utility upgrades an existing Greenplum Database 
3.x system to 3.2. It can also be used to downgrade a 3.2 system 
back to 3.1 or 3.0. This utility updates the system catalog and 
internal version number, but not the actual software binaries.

If your Greenplum Database system has a standby master host 
configured, the gpmigrator utility will not upgrade the standby 
master. It will remove the standby master from your system 
configuration and then you must re-add it back to your 
system after the upgrade is complete.

*****************************************************
OPTIONS
*****************************************************

<old_GPHOME_path>

Required. The absolute path to the current version of 
Greenplum Database software you want to migrate away from.


<new_GPHOME_path>

Required. The absolute path to the new version of Greenplum 
Database software you want to migrate to.


-d <master_data_directory>

Optional. The master host data directory. If not specified, 
the value set for $MASTER_DATA_DIRECTORY will be used.


-l <logfile_directory>

The directory to write the log file. Defaults to ~/gpAdminLogs.


-q (quiet mode)

Run in quiet mode. Command output is not displayed on the screen, 
but is still written to the log file.


--help

Displays the online help.


--version

Displays the version of this utility. 


*****************************************************
EXAMPLES
*****************************************************

First make sure you are using the 3.2 version of the Greenplum 
utilities:

export GPHOME=/usr/local/greenplum-db-3.2.0.0


Upgrade to version 3.2 from version 3.1.1.5:

gpmigrator /usr/local/greenplum-db-3.1.1.5 /usr/local/greenplum-db-3.2.0.0


